cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sentinel Seismik (quake-id): Real-Time Indonesia Earthquake Fusion & Tectonic Regime Classifier"
message: "If you use this software or methodology in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fajrianshah"
    given-names: "Evans Azka"
    affiliation: "National Research and Innovation Agency (BRIN); Graduate School, Universitas Gadjah Mada"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: MIT
url: "https://quake.transbulent.id"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gisrad/quake-id"
abstract: >-
  Real-time 3D WebGIS platform and Cloudflare edge ingestion pipeline fusing BMKG InaTEWS SeisComP and MMI felt-intensity bulletins with the USGS ComCat earthquake catalog across Indonesia. Classifies hypocenters into shallow crustal fault, subduction megathrust, and deep Wadati-Benioff intraslab regimes across 16 mapped Indonesian tectonic structures, with an interactive longitude-depth cross-section and offline historical replays for the 2018 Palu and Lombok sequences.
keywords:
  - earthquake
  - indonesia
  - bmkg
  - usgs
  - seismology
  - megathrust
  - active-faults
  - wadati-benioff
  - cloudflare-workers
  - maplibre-gl
